    "Paragraph 3 ends: the question 'sounds naive, because everyone inside knows that it always has'. Repeated deviation has become normal practice, so a question about it appears to show ignorance rather than insight.",
    "Assuming that the outsider must be ignorant, rather than that the insiders have adjusted their sense of normal.",
    "The reason is given in the same sentence.",
